---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What ReaderTweaks is, how the guides are researched and kept current, and how the site is funded."
  path="/about/"
  activeNav="about"
  jsonLd={breadcrumbJsonLd([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
  ])}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>ReaderTweaks</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A practical reference for getting more out of your e-reader, organised by
        the exact device you own.
      </p>

      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        Every e-reader we cover has its own hub, and each hub has the same seven
        sections: Guides, KOReader, Calibre, Customization, Troubleshooting,
        Accessories and Comparisons. When you search for a problem on a specific
        device, the page you land on should be written for that device, not for
        e-readers in general.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside the device hubs, the <a href="/guides/">guides section</a>
        covers the topics that apply to every reader: ebook formats, Calibre, and
        KOReader setup.
      </p>

      <h2 id="method">How the guides are researched</h2>
      <p>
        Each guide is built from primary sources: manufacturers' own help centres
        and specifications, developer documentation, and the official
        instructions and release notes published by the software projects
        themselves, such as KOReader and Calibre. Where the official material is
        thin, we cross-check community documentation from the maintainers of
        those tools, and we aim to make clear on the page when something rests on
        community information rather than an official source.
      </p>
      <p>
        E-reader software changes often, and an instruction that was right six
        months ago can be wrong today. So guides state the software version they
        were written against wherever it matters, and every page shows the date it
        was last updated. We revisit pages
        when a significant update lands — a new firmware release, a new jailbreak,
        a change to an install method — and where the current position is unclear
        or unconfirmed, we say that plainly rather than guess.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you find something wrong or out of date, please tell us at
        <a href="mailto:hello@readertweaks.com">hello@readertweaks.com</a>.
        Corrections are treated as a priority.
      </p>

      <h2 id="funding">How ReaderTweaks is funded</h2>
      <p>
        ReaderTweaks is an independent commercial publication and may earn a small
        commission on purchases made through our affiliate links.
      </p>

      <h3>Affiliate links</h3>
      <p>
        Device and accessory links go to Amazon and carry our Amazon Associates
        tag. As an Amazon Associate, ReaderTweaks earns from qualifying purchases.
        If you buy through one of these links, we may earn a small commission at
        no extra cost to you. We recommend a product because it is the right one
        for the job, and we disclose the link because you should know it can earn
        us something. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> covers the data
        side.
      </p>

      <h2 id="boundaries">What we will not do</h2>
      <p>No amount of money buys any of the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A positive review, or guaranteed favourable coverage.</li>
        <li>A ranking, or the top spot in an independent comparison.</li>
        <li>A change to troubleshooting advice.</li>
        <li>A recommendation that is not disclosed as sponsored.</li>
        <li>
          Manufacturer control over an editorial conclusion, pre-approval of an
          independent review, or a veto over legitimate criticism.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="contact">Media, advertising and partnerships</h2>
      <p>
        Advertisers, manufacturers, retailers, PR and media contacts, and
        potential partners are welcome to get in touch:
        <a href="mailto:hello@readertweaks.com">hello@readertweaks.com</a>. We are
        happy to talk about ad placements, sponsorships, review units and
        partnerships.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any arrangement we make sits alongside our editorial independence rather
        than in place of it: our coverage, verdicts and rankings stay our own.
      </p>
      <p>
        Corrections and reader suggestions go to the same address.
      </p>

      <h2 id="independence">Independence and ownership</h2>
      <p>
        ReaderTweaks is independently owned and not affiliated with Kobo, Amazon,
        Onyx, PocketBook, reMarkable or any other manufacturer. Product names are
        used for identification only. No manufacturer or advertiser has a stake
        in the site or a say in what it publishes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; }
  .prose h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
